  3564                                  ; netdiag_dump_tx: prints, for the RTL8168 path, the PCI Status register
  3565                                  ; (config offset 0x04, upper 16 bits - Master/Target Abort and parity error
  3566                                  ; bits live here) and the raw failed TX descriptor's command dword plus a
  3567                                  ; fresh TPPoll readback. This is diagnostic only - it tells us whether the
  3568                                  ; hardware itself is reporting a bus-level error (abort/parity) versus the
  3569                                  ; descriptor engine silently never touching the slot at all, which are two
  3570                                  ; very different bugs that "TX error" alone can't distinguish.
  3571                                  netdiag_dump_tx:
