  3613                                      ; Status bits (8/11/12/13/14/15) are write-1-to-clear; Command (low 16)
  3614                                      ; is plain RW. Writing back exactly what we just read clears any latched
  3615                                      ; error bits without touching Command, so the NEXT dump reflects fresh
  3616                                      ; state instead of re-showing the same abort forever after the first
