  7130                                  ; ============================================================
  7131                                  ;  Aliases ("ali <name> <commands>")
  7132                                  ;
  7133                                  ;  An alias binds a name to an arbitrary command string (which may
  7134                                  ;  itself contain ; chains and a ~ pipe). Defining one is intercepted
  7135                                  ;  as raw text before ; splitting ever sees it (try_handle_ali_line,
  7136                                  ;  called from the interactive shell loop and from cmd_rr's script
  7137                                  ;  loop); invoking one happens inside dispatch, when cmd_buf doesn't
  7138                                  ;  match any built-in command but does match an alias name.
  7139                                  ; ============================================================
  7140                                  
  7141                                  ; try_handle_ali_line: line_buf holds a raw, not-yet-tokenized input
  7142                                  ; line. If it starts with the exact word "ali" followed by a name and
  7143                                  ; at least one command, stores the alias and returns al=1 (caller
  7144                                  ; should treat the line as fully handled and not process it further).
  7145                                  ; Otherwise returns al=0 and leaves line_buf untouched, so the caller
  7146                                  ; processes the line normally.
