  7344                                  ; cmd_alias_invoke: called from dispatch when cmd_buf matched an alias
  7345                                  ; name, with [alias_match_idx] set to that alias's table index. Runs
  7346                                  ; the alias's stored body exactly like a freshly-typed line, through
  7347                                  ; the same chain processor (process_chain or process_chain_rr) that's
  7348                                  ; currently active, so ; chaining and ~ piping inside the alias work
  7349                                  ; normally and nested alias calls work too.
  7350                                  ;
  7351                                  ; This has to protect two pieces of global, shared state that would
  7352                                  ; otherwise be clobbered by that nested call:
  7353                                  ;   - chain_scan_buf: the outer process_chain(_rr) is still mid-scan
  7354                                  ;     over it (via r12/r13), so it's backed up on the stack, restored
  7355                                  ;     after the nested call returns. r12/r13 are ordinary registers,
  7356                                  ;     saved/restored by normal callee-saved discipline, so only the
  7357                                  ;     memory needs protecting, not the pointers themselves.
  7358                                  ;   - chain_is_rr: process_chain/process_chain_rr each set this as a
  7359                                  ;     side effect, so it's saved and restored too, otherwise an alias
  7360                                  ;     call partway through an rr script could leave later segments in
  7361                                  ;     that script using the wrong dispatch-wrapping behaviour.
