 11048                                      ; --- REWRITE: do a real, standard RTL8168-style bring-up instead of
 11049                                      ; the earlier "skip reset, hope the board firmware already configured
 11050                                      ; it" workaround. That workaround was based on the theory that this
 11051                                      ; 8168E+ chip needs vendor microcode this driver can't upload, so
 11052                                      ; touching config registers would only break whatever good state
 11053                                      ; existed. In practice it got RX/DHCP working but TX never got out of
 11054                                      ; a confirmed, repeatable PCI Signaled Target-Abort on every send -
 11055                                      ; i.e. TX was never actually in a known-good state to begin with, so
 11056                                      ; there was nothing worth preserving on that side. A proper reset +
 11057                                      ; full descriptor/TCR/RCR/CPCMD programming (the same sequence real
 11058                                      ; r8169-family drivers do) is more likely to leave the TX DMA engine
 11059                                      ; in a state this driver's simple descriptor ring can actually drive,
 11060                                      ; even without the full microcode upload.
 11061                                      ;
 11062                                      ; unlock config registers (9346CR) before touching CMD/TCR/etc.
 11063 00019015 8B3C25[B0E80500]            mov edi, [nic_io_base]
