 11098                                      ; Kick the PHY: on some real boards it comes up in (or gets left in,
 11099                                      ; by firmware) a powered-down/not-negotiating state that the MAC-side
 11100                                      ; soft reset above never touches, since RST only resets the MAC, not
 11101                                      ; the PHY. Without this, RTL_IO_PHYSTATUS's link bit can simply never
 11102                                      ; assert - .rtl_link_wait below then always burns its whole ~5s budget
 11103                                      ; and falls through with no link, which is silent (nic_present still
 11104                                      ; gets set) but means every frame this driver sends from here on is
 11105                                      ; just dropped, and every "tcp"/ping/dhcp call ends up hanging until
 11106                                      ; its own retry budget in turn expires. Do this now, before the link
 11107                                      ; wait, so autonegotiation has the whole ring-setup sequence below to
 11108                                      ; run concurrently with it instead of starting cold right before we
