 11244                                  
 11245                                      ; wait for the copper link to actually come up before handing the NIC
 11246                                      ; to the rest of the stack. QEMU's virtual link is always already "up",
 11247                                      ; which is why this was never needed there - real Gigabit autonegotiation
 11248                                      ; plus switch-port bring-up (STP listening/learning, etc.) commonly takes
 11249                                      ; several seconds, and frames sent before the link is up are just dropped.
 11250                                      ; ~5s budget (500 * ~10ms); if it times out we still proceed - nic_present
 11251                                      ; is still set below so a late link-up will work once dhcp/ping retry.
 11252 0001923D 41B9F4010000                mov r9d, 500
