 11663                                      ; Wait for the chip to clear OWN on this slot. QEMU clears it almost
 11664                                      ; immediately, so a raw loop count worked there; on real hardware the
 11665                                      ; first TX DMA after link bring-up can take far longer than a cached-
 11666                                      ; RAM spin allows (the loop reads the descriptor from the CPU cache,
 11667                                      ; which outruns the NIC's write-back by orders of magnitude). So wait
 11668                                      ; on wall-clock RTC seconds instead: up to ~2s, re-kicking TPPoll each
 11669                                      ; second in case the chip needed another poll to notice the slot.
 11670                                      ; NOTE: budget is in whole-second ticks, but the tick boundary itself
 11671                                      ; consumes no polling time - see the js/jz fix below. With r11d=N we
 11672                                      ; get the remainder of the current second plus N full subsequent
 11673                                      ; seconds of continuous OWN polling before giving up. Bumped from 2 to
 11674                                      ; 5: field reports on real hardware still showed OWN clearing (and
 11675                                      ; NPQ already down) moments after a "failure" even with the earlier
 11676                                      ; 2-3s budget, especially around ring wraparound (EOR slot) - so the
 11677                                      ; occasional real-world completion is simply slower than that.
 11678 0001963B E887EFFFFF                  call rtc_sec_now
 11679 00019640 4189C1                      mov r9d, eax
 11680 00019643 880425[8CA40600]            mov [nic_tx_wait_start], al   ; true start second, kept separate from r9d
 11681                                                                    ; (which gets overwritten every tick below) -
 11682                                                                    ; so netdiag_dump_tx can report real elapsed
 11683                                                                    ; wall-clock time on failure, not just a tick
 11684                                                                    ; count that's always the same constant.
 11685                                      ; Bumped 5 -> 20: with rtc_sec_now's BCD bug fixed we can finally trust
 11686                                      ; the elapsed-time diagnostic, but the last two runs still failed with
 11687                                      ; an identical signature (no PCI error, NPQ/OWN both eventually clear)
 11688                                      ; even after padding ruled out short-frame handling as the cause. That
 11689                                      ; points at this chip/link genuinely needing longer than 5-6s for its
 11690                                      ; first TX after an idle gap (e.g. PHY/EEE low-power wake, or link
 11691                                      ; re-training) rather than a logic bug in the wait itself. Widening
 11692                                      ; the budget is a cheap way to confirm that: if this send now
 11693                                      ; succeeds, the real elapsed-seconds print (now trustworthy) tells us
 11694                                      ; how much headroom this hardware actually needs so the budget can be
 11695                                      ; set correctly instead of guessed at again.
