   904                              <1> ; party_bg_suspend: cooperative yield. Called from party_exec_stmts at a
   905                              <1> ; statement boundary when the background quantum is exhausted (see the
   906                              <1> ; party_bg_active / party_bg_quantum check at the top of the statement
   907                              <1> ; loop). Parks the interpreter state (globals + r13/r14/r15) into the
   908                              <1> ; current process's ctx area, saves the private-stack pointer (its top
   909                              <1> ; word is the resume address - the instruction right after this call) into
   910                              <1> ; proc_bg_rsp[slot], then switches back to the scheduler's stack and
   911                              <1> ; returns to bg_scheduler_tick. The next bg_step_proc restores the ctx,
   912                              <1> ; sets rsp back to proc_bg_rsp[slot] and RETs, so execution continues
   913                              <1> ; right after this call. Clobbers rax, rbx, rcx, rsi, rdi, r8-r15.
