  1095                              <1> .pes_not_killed:
  1096                              <1>     ; Cooperative background yield: when this interpreter is running as a
  1097                              <1>     ; stepped background process, count the statement and hand control back
  1098                              <1>     ; to the scheduler once party_bg_quantum is exhausted. party_bg_active
  1099                              <1>     ; is 1 only while bg_step_proc is driving us - a foreground party/run
  1100                              <1>     ; never yields here. On resume the scheduler has reset party_bg_quantum
  1101                              <1>     ; and party_bg_suspend drops us back at this exact statement boundary.
