   684                              <1>     ; this distinguishes a bus-level error (abort/parity) from the descriptor
   685                              <1>     ; engine silently never touching the slot. Only meaningful for a genuine
   686                              <1>     ; raw-TX failure, so skip it entirely for the no-reply case above.
