 15734                                  ; read_line: rdi=buffer, rcx=max chars. Echoes to screen, handles
 15735                                  ; backspace/Delete, Left/Right/Home/End in-line cursor movement, Up/Down
 15736                                  ; command history, and terminates on Enter. Buffer is null terminated.
 15737                                  ; r8 = current line length, r9 = buffer ptr, r10 = max chars, r11 = the
 15738                                  ; cursor's position within the line (0..r8) - everything below that
 15739                                  ; isn't a straight end-of-line append goes through r11 instead of r8.
 15740                                  ; read_char_or_step: like get_char but non-blocking from the shell's
 15741                                  ; point of view: if no keyboard byte is waiting, steps the background
 15742                                  ; processes for one quantum and returns al = 0 (never returned by
 15743                                  ; get_char, which maps every zero table entry to "wait"). Preserves
 15744                                  ; every register so read_line's r8-r11 line state survives a step.
 15745                                  read_char_or_step:
